WEBVTT

01:41.550 --> 01:48.230
Op.11 The Future, Dreams, Thank You — And!

01:44.360 --> 01:46.020
I love you, Otoya.

01:46.500 --> 01:48.710
My dear Otoya.

01:55.360 --> 01:56.910
I'll do my best.

01:57.630 --> 02:02.070
I'll shine like the sun
and illuminate everyone as an idol.

02:02.890 --> 02:04.560
I'll make everyone smile.

02:05.840 --> 02:09.520
You just watch me, Auntie.

02:13.650 --> 02:14.430
Otoya.

02:43.050 --> 02:44.260
Guys.

02:45.420 --> 02:46.290
Otoya.

02:47.240 --> 02:51.060
We were really worried about you.

03:05.280 --> 03:06.320
I'm sorry!

03:08.940 --> 03:10.090
It's true.

03:10.750 --> 03:11.500
But...

03:13.040 --> 03:15.090
Looks like we don't need
to worry now.

03:16.180 --> 03:16.890
Yeah.

03:20.150 --> 03:22.300
But how did you guys find me?

03:22.950 --> 03:28.560
The orphanage director told us
you had a promise you failed to keep.

03:29.960 --> 03:34.150
We wanted to see this place
where you'd promise to meet, too.

03:34.150 --> 03:39.780
We all agreed we wanted
to be here for your important moment.

03:39.780 --> 03:43.270
As friends bonded together.

03:54.630 --> 03:58.050
Sorry. I'm sorry, guys.

03:58.050 --> 04:00.380
You have nothing to apologize for.

04:00.800 --> 04:05.300
Otoya, I'm the one who needs to apologize.

04:05.300 --> 04:05.890
What?

04:07.080 --> 04:11.020
We've been rooming together
since we were students,

04:11.790 --> 04:14.560
but I didn't realize how you felt.

04:15.090 --> 04:16.480
But I...

04:16.480 --> 04:20.540
We all have pasts that make us who we are.

04:21.350 --> 04:24.490
We can't share all of our pasts
with each other.

04:24.490 --> 04:28.030
But we can try to understand each other.

04:29.310 --> 04:34.640
Should anything happen in the future,
I'm sure we can overcome it.

04:35.820 --> 04:38.860
That's right. That's the
kind of friends we are.

04:38.860 --> 04:39.790
Right?

04:40.300 --> 04:41.300
Yeah.

04:42.250 --> 04:47.840
When the decisive concert was
announced, I said STARISH is eternal.

04:48.430 --> 04:50.510
That we'd be able to walk
together forever and ever.

04:51.920 --> 04:54.410
But now I think

04:55.630 --> 04:57.730
there may be no such thing as eternity.

04:59.630 --> 05:05.980
After all, nobody knows
what's going to happen in the future.

05:07.880 --> 05:11.740
We may not be able
to keep working as STARISH.

05:13.410 --> 05:15.640
But that's why...

05:16.580 --> 05:18.650
Because it's not eternal,
that's what makes it great.

05:19.920 --> 05:21.500
That's how I feel now.

05:22.330 --> 05:23.300
Otoya.

05:23.300 --> 05:30.370
You're correct. Right now, we're sharing
these moments together as STARISH.

05:30.370 --> 05:36.880
With our separate pasts, we're here now,
making the same music together.

05:36.880 --> 05:38.230
It's amazing.

05:38.230 --> 05:40.140
It's a miracle.

05:40.570 --> 05:44.320
We were granted these miraculous
moments by the muses.

05:44.320 --> 05:48.550
But that time is not limitless, but limited.

05:48.550 --> 05:53.600
That's why we should treasure every moment.

05:53.600 --> 05:58.870
Yeah. Let's always go all out,
so we don't have any regrets.

05:58.870 --> 06:00.980
Yeah. I'm happy, guys.

06:01.760 --> 06:03.310
I'm so happy.

06:04.280 --> 06:07.000
I'm so happy to be here with you now.

06:19.680 --> 06:22.060
Nothing beats your smiles, Otoya.

06:22.380 --> 06:24.650
It's truly the smile of an idol.

06:24.650 --> 06:25.530
Yeah.

06:25.530 --> 06:28.150
It's a smile that puts
a smile on everyone's face.

06:31.830 --> 06:34.240
I can't sit still anymore!

06:34.240 --> 06:37.120
Yeah! I'm feeling restless!

06:37.120 --> 06:39.710
Yeah! I feel like running!

06:40.090 --> 06:41.310
Let's run!

06:45.380 --> 06:47.420
Let's go to the Song Festa!

06:58.180 --> 07:02.440
Let's run, run down the road we believe in

07:02.440 --> 07:06.840
Above us is a vast blue sky

07:06.840 --> 07:10.780
The buds of dreams born from tomorrow

07:10.780 --> 07:15.200
Become the lights that make today bloom

07:15.200 --> 07:18.830
When the darkness frightens you

07:18.830 --> 07:23.190
Reach out your hands

07:23.190 --> 07:27.170
We can lean on each other and scream out

07:27.170 --> 07:30.980
Let's run again

07:31.930 --> 07:36.010
On the map to the future

07:34.930 --> 07:36.010
I just saw STARISH running

07:36.350 --> 07:40.480
Our dreams and bonds

07:39.390 --> 07:40.480
Where!?

07:39.390 --> 07:40.480
Kinshicho!!!

07:40.480 --> 07:44.440
These days full of gratitude

07:44.440 --> 07:47.900
We'll bundle them all together

07:47.900 --> 07:49.230
And then

07:49.230 --> 07:57.530
The words I still haven't been
able to use yet burn in my heart

07:57.530 --> 08:02.150
The seven-colored rainbow wasn't meant to be

08:02.150 --> 08:05.540
There's a color missing from it

08:05.540 --> 08:09.300
Those words are the future

08:09.300 --> 08:17.250
A miraculous legend we create together

08:17.890 --> 08:26.430
Always we can

08:32.860 --> 08:36.780
By the way, Ikki, we heard
your duet project song.

08:36.780 --> 08:38.780
It was amazing.

08:38.780 --> 08:42.040
I had no idea you could sing like that.

08:42.040 --> 08:44.010
I didn't know, either.

08:44.470 --> 08:47.570
It was a little too intense for me.

08:48.130 --> 08:52.050
But... I like that song.

08:52.050 --> 08:56.510
Now, I'm genuinely glad
I was able to sing it.

08:57.010 --> 08:59.430
Thanks for the amazing song, Nanami.

08:59.960 --> 09:02.640
No, thank you.

09:02.640 --> 09:04.350
I'm so glad.

09:04.350 --> 09:05.690
Yeah.

09:05.690 --> 09:09.270
Now all of the duet projects
have been completed.

09:09.620 --> 09:12.420
Honestly, it was hard.

09:12.420 --> 09:15.570
But I'm glad we did it.

09:15.880 --> 09:21.660
I honestly believe each of us
overcame something and grew.

09:21.660 --> 09:22.760
You're right.

09:23.500 --> 09:27.220
Now we can sing songs
we couldn't have sung before.

09:27.220 --> 09:29.170
We have that confidence now.

09:29.170 --> 09:29.990
Yeah.

09:31.400 --> 09:33.000
It's almost time.

09:33.000 --> 09:35.170
For the Triple S decisive concert.

09:36.930 --> 09:40.070
I heard QUARTET NIGHT is already rehearsing.

09:40.070 --> 09:44.680
Yes, and I just started meeting with HEAVENS.

09:44.680 --> 09:46.560
It's our turn next.

09:46.560 --> 09:48.290
Our hearts must be as one.

09:48.910 --> 09:52.620
Let's make it a superb song
that only we can sing.

09:52.620 --> 09:53.480
Yeah.

09:54.090 --> 09:55.030
Excuse me...

09:55.610 --> 10:00.070
While I was thinking about all of you,
a melody came into my head.

10:00.070 --> 10:01.780
Our song?

10:01.780 --> 10:02.740
Yes.

10:04.020 --> 10:05.540
Of course.

10:05.540 --> 10:08.960
There's no way Otoya wouldn't return.

10:08.960 --> 10:10.920
I know everything.

10:13.800 --> 10:16.930
He was actually pretty worried about him.

10:16.930 --> 10:17.910
I know.

10:17.910 --> 10:21.100
Boy, I'm excited to sing your song.

10:21.660 --> 10:24.220
A song to melt bodies and hearts.

10:24.220 --> 10:25.470
I'm counting on you.

10:25.470 --> 10:26.980
Okay.

10:27.340 --> 10:30.110
That was a fulfilling meeting.

10:30.110 --> 10:34.400
Only me, the cutest boy in the universe,
and HEAVENS will be able to sing this song.

10:35.520 --> 10:38.360
A song to convey the waves of heaven.

10:38.360 --> 10:40.400
An explosive song!

10:40.400 --> 10:41.490
Okay.

10:41.490 --> 10:43.450
I should get going.

10:43.450 --> 10:47.660
I'll complete the song based on today's
meeting and send it to you when I'm finished.

10:47.660 --> 10:48.580
Sure.

10:49.680 --> 10:51.200
I'm looking forward to it.

10:51.200 --> 10:51.950
Okay.

10:53.920 --> 10:56.250
The president is calling you!

11:02.260 --> 11:03.300
STARISH appears on music show!!

11:02.660 --> 11:05.390
What is the meaning of this, Eiichi?

11:03.300 --> 11:05.390
Is HEAVENS at a disadvantage??

11:05.750 --> 11:09.040
I thought you crushed Ittoki Otoya.

11:09.610 --> 11:10.710
Crushed him?

11:11.390 --> 11:14.360
I simply aimed to create
the ultimate song with Ittoki Otoya.

11:15.320 --> 11:16.720
You're working with them?

11:17.460 --> 11:21.070
You're nothing more than my tools.

11:22.020 --> 11:22.770
Tools?

11:22.770 --> 11:23.900
What does that mean?

11:24.640 --> 11:26.970
Is HEAVENS at a disadvantage??

11:24.640 --> 11:27.420
I expect nothing from you now.

11:24.640 --> 11:29.070
STARISH appears on music show!!

11:24.640 --> 11:29.070
A Dazzling Break

11:26.970 --> 11:29.070
Sudden Appearance In Plain Clothes!

11:27.420 --> 11:29.070
I will make us win.

11:29.070 --> 11:31.180
You shouldn't undervalue us.

11:31.180 --> 11:36.510
Yeah. We'll beat STARISH and
QUARTET NIGHT, fair and square.

11:36.510 --> 11:38.490
We require no intervention.

11:38.490 --> 11:40.590
We are confident.

11:40.590 --> 11:42.010
We will win!

11:42.010 --> 11:45.470
Quiet, losers!

11:47.360 --> 11:49.020
Losers?

11:49.020 --> 11:50.520
You're the loser!

11:51.950 --> 11:56.770
You and Shining Saotome once competed
fiercely against each other.

11:58.400 --> 12:04.120
With "Love is Dead", you set a record
of nineteen million copies sold.

12:05.470 --> 12:07.480
Believing you'd won, you retired.

12:09.410 --> 12:15.000
But Shining Saotome sold
twenty million copies of <i>For Love</i>.

12:19.040 --> 12:21.260
You suffered a total loss.

12:23.240 --> 12:25.800
We're not tools for your revenge.

12:26.660 --> 12:27.390
Shut up!

12:28.970 --> 12:31.630
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

12:31.630 --> 12:34.780
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

12:34.780 --> 12:37.650
Shut up!

12:43.050 --> 12:49.230
Since that hateful day, I have lived
only to achieve one goal.

12:51.530 --> 12:59.210
To send him down into a pit of despair
through my complete and total victory.

13:00.380 --> 13:05.840
I won't allow my pets to get in my way.

13:06.220 --> 13:08.550
I won't allow it!

13:16.190 --> 13:19.900
It's been a while since
we last performed with HEAVENS.

13:19.900 --> 13:23.320
We did meet up individually
during the duet project.

13:23.320 --> 13:27.280
With the decisive concert coming up,
let's really show them what we can do.

13:27.750 --> 13:28.980
Let's do our best.

13:30.760 --> 13:32.130
Good morning.

13:32.130 --> 13:32.700
Good morning.

13:32.700 --> 13:33.920
Good morning.

13:34.830 --> 13:37.020
Is HEAVENS not here yet?

13:37.020 --> 13:42.160
They just called to cancel
their appearance today.

13:42.160 --> 13:43.070
What?

13:43.070 --> 13:44.270
Cancel?

13:44.270 --> 13:45.680
What is the meaning of this?

13:46.220 --> 13:48.010
Good morning.

13:49.160 --> 13:49.720
Huh?

13:50.030 --> 13:51.970
Shion's not here yet?

13:51.970 --> 13:53.200
I'm sorry.

13:53.630 --> 13:57.000
We'll be conducting
a solo interview with you today.

13:57.000 --> 14:02.190
What? But didn't you primarily
want to discuss the duet project?

14:02.190 --> 14:07.820
Yes, but Raging Entertainment
called to cancel.

14:08.570 --> 14:10.450
The meeting is canceled?

14:10.450 --> 14:13.450
But nobody told me.

14:13.450 --> 14:16.980
In any case, that's what I
was told by the project manager.

14:16.980 --> 14:18.560
But why?

14:19.080 --> 14:21.000
It's an important new song for them.

14:21.000 --> 14:22.670
There's nothing I can tell you.

14:26.100 --> 14:28.720
What do you mean by "the plan is on hold?"

14:28.720 --> 14:32.950
Wasn't the embargo on discussing the
<i> Fire and Wind</i> sequel going to be lifted soon?

14:34.140 --> 14:36.490
What? You can't discuss the situation?

14:37.410 --> 14:39.070
What's going on?

14:39.980 --> 14:45.190
HEAVENS Exiled From the Industry!?

14:45.190 --> 14:46.360
What happened to HEAVENS!?

14:46.360 --> 14:47.440
What will happen to the
Triple S decisive concert?!

14:48.700 --> 14:50.300
Did HEAVENS disappear?

14:48.880 --> 14:51.230
This is crazy! In a bad way!

14:50.510 --> 14:51.230
Is this the dark side of
the entertainment industry?

14:51.230 --> 14:52.600
The truth is

14:52.600 --> 14:53.440
Shrouded in mystery

14:54.170 --> 14:56.830
They've canceled all of their appearances.

14:56.830 --> 15:00.250
They're not answering
their phones or e-mails, either.

15:00.250 --> 15:04.090
No way. What on earth
is happening to HEAVENS?

15:04.700 --> 15:07.110
It must be Raging Otori.

15:07.110 --> 15:08.800
That's exactly right.

15:08.800 --> 15:11.670
Raging Otori is behind all of this.

15:13.430 --> 15:15.940
It's not something that
should happen, though.

15:15.940 --> 15:17.840
But why?

15:17.840 --> 15:20.680
It's an important time for us
with the decisive concert coming up.

15:20.680 --> 15:22.310
What good does any of this do?

15:22.890 --> 15:26.320
Apparently, HEAVENS defied him.

15:26.320 --> 15:27.610
Defied him?

15:28.500 --> 15:32.330
That's the kind of man
Raging Otori has always been.

15:32.330 --> 15:35.120
He wants everything to go his way.

15:35.470 --> 15:37.520
He won't allow anyone to defy him.

15:37.520 --> 15:38.620
No way.

15:42.880 --> 15:47.260
Will they be unable to appear
in the Triple S decisive concert?

15:50.780 --> 15:51.590
Possibly not.

15:56.230 --> 15:57.690
That's cruel.

15:57.690 --> 15:59.270
That's too cruel.

16:00.210 --> 16:01.420
Too cruel.

16:02.780 --> 16:07.230
What do you suppose HEAVENS
is doing right now?

16:10.090 --> 16:11.400
Excuse me.

16:12.000 --> 16:13.340
I have a request.

16:23.870 --> 16:25.690
Damn it!

16:25.690 --> 16:27.500
What the hell is this?

16:29.340 --> 16:34.580
With the path closed,
we have become captives.

16:35.720 --> 16:37.360
I was naive.

16:37.920 --> 16:41.270
I didn't think Dad would go this far.

16:41.270 --> 16:43.630
It's not normal.

16:41.270 --> 16:44.520
Did HEAVENS disappear?

16:41.270 --> 16:44.520
This is crazy! In a bad way

16:41.270 --> 16:44.520
Is this the dark side
of the entertainment industry?

16:41.270 --> 16:44.520
The truth is
shrouded in mystery

16:44.520 --> 16:46.770
It'll damage the agency's reputation.

16:46.770 --> 16:49.730
But he did it anyway.

16:49.730 --> 16:55.570
"If the cuckoo does not sing, kill it."

16:56.720 --> 16:58.680
His power is absolute.

16:59.310 --> 17:01.080
He's coming to kill us.

17:01.080 --> 17:05.370
In other words, we won't be
performing at the decisive concert.

17:06.170 --> 17:09.170
Do we have to give in?

17:11.600 --> 17:13.990
If we steel our hearts and apologize...

17:15.880 --> 17:21.140
We can perform at the decisive concert.

17:23.450 --> 17:24.480
We can't do that.

17:25.510 --> 17:28.020
It would be a defilement of music.

17:28.820 --> 17:33.390
They're right. We can't give up
what's most important to us.

17:42.930 --> 17:44.870
Damn it!

17:45.270 --> 17:46.820
What are we supposed to do?

17:54.010 --> 17:55.410
Wh-What's going on?

17:56.710 --> 17:57.630
The power's out.

17:57.630 --> 17:59.260
What about the backup generator?

17:59.260 --> 18:00.970
It's not working.

18:03.260 --> 18:04.220
We apologize for the sudden intrusion.

18:32.250 --> 18:33.760
STARISH?

18:33.760 --> 18:34.900
Why?

18:34.900 --> 18:36.340
What do you want?

18:38.010 --> 18:39.880
You guys look miserable.

18:39.880 --> 18:40.510
What?

18:40.510 --> 18:41.730
Why did you come here?

18:41.730 --> 18:43.140
Did you come to brag?

18:43.140 --> 18:46.020
To mock our despair?

18:47.560 --> 18:49.810
You sound surprisingly defeated.

18:50.400 --> 18:52.810
Have you given up on the decisive concert?

18:54.000 --> 18:55.280
Are you not performing?

18:55.620 --> 18:59.990
Is that how little you
cared about the Triple S?

18:59.990 --> 19:02.320
You don't understand.

19:14.510 --> 19:16.380
Nanami asked us to bring this to you.

19:17.570 --> 19:19.340
This is HEAVENS' song for the concert!

19:31.300 --> 19:32.810
We'll be waiting!

20:17.770 --> 20:24.030
What HEAVENS needs now is hope,
and to not give up.

20:24.440 --> 20:27.770
Haruka's song will give them strength.

20:27.770 --> 20:31.700
Nanami's songs have always cheered us up.

20:31.700 --> 20:35.090
Yeah, and saved us.

20:35.090 --> 20:36.670
And given us courage.

20:36.670 --> 20:38.530
The same must be true for HEAVENS.

20:39.190 --> 20:40.960
I know they can do it.

20:52.520 --> 20:53.940
Good!

20:54.340 --> 20:55.870
I want to sing!

20:55.870 --> 20:58.150
How could we not sing this song?

20:59.270 --> 21:01.970
We mustn't abandon hope yet.

21:01.970 --> 21:03.860
I'm beginning to feel that way.

21:03.860 --> 21:07.330
You're right. If we give up, it's all over.

21:07.330 --> 21:10.140
But if we don't give up...

21:10.140 --> 21:12.450
There is a way.

21:12.450 --> 21:16.520
All right. Let's write some
super cute lyrics to this song.

21:16.520 --> 21:17.420
Yeah.

21:17.420 --> 21:19.040
Let's start right away!

21:19.040 --> 21:20.530
Yeah!

21:21.300 --> 21:23.710
Good!

21:24.860 --> 21:27.760
I want to believe in the
power of music, don't you?

21:28.770 --> 21:31.300
I'm sure they'll get back up.

21:31.300 --> 21:35.030
Raging Otori's actions were exceedingly rude.

21:35.600 --> 21:40.730
We declined our victory
so we could compete as a group.

21:40.730 --> 21:44.300
Yeah, and he won't let HEAVENS perform?

21:44.300 --> 21:45.360
He can't be serious.

21:46.230 --> 21:47.670
I don't have the data,

21:47.670 --> 21:50.030
but everyone besides
Raging Otori wants to see

21:50.400 --> 21:53.750
all three groups at the concert, right?

21:54.900 --> 21:59.150
All our hearts were drawn to music.

21:59.150 --> 22:01.340
All of us believe in music.

22:05.340 --> 22:08.110
QUARTET NIGHT.

22:10.960 --> 22:12.200
STARISH.

22:18.900 --> 22:20.020
HEAVENS.

22:24.740 --> 22:28.960
We'll be at that concert,
no matter what.

24:06.470 --> 24:08.840
I'll never forget what happened today.

24:08.840 --> 24:09.840
Uta Pri!
